<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Codex Zouche-Nuttall</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Codex Zouche-Nuttall is a pre-Hispanic Mixtec <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> painted on deerskin and folded like a screen, now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-museum">British Museum</a>. One side records the histories of several Mixtec centres, the other the life and conquests of the 11th-century ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eight-deer-jaguar-claw">Eight Deer Jaguar Claw</a> of Tilantongo. It is named after Zelia Nuttall, who published it in 1902, and Baron Zouche, a former owner.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/codex-zouche-nuttall.jpg" alt="Codex Zouche-Nuttall" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codex_Zouche-Nuttall,_page_20.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
